; Install-script policy (npm >= 11.16, RFC npm/rfcs#868).
;
; npm resolves the effective policy from, highest precedence first:
;   1. --allow-scripts on the CLI  (an ERROR for project-scoped install/ci --
;      never pass it in CI)
;   2. the root package.json "allowScripts" field
;   3. this .npmrc
;
; The root package.json declares "allowScripts" so required native packages can
; be approved while optional install-time optimizers such as workerd are denied.
; Keep the full list there: npm ignores any .npmrc allow-scripts value when the
; package field is present.
;
; Why it is needed: better-sqlite3 is a native module and compiles (or fetches
; a prebuild) in its install script; esbuild and @swc/core unpack platform
; binaries; msgpackr-extract selects or builds its optional native accelerator.
; workerd ships a platform package and functions without its postinstall
; launch-path optimization, so its script stays disabled.
;
; strict-allow-scripts turns every install script outside this reviewed policy
; into a hard failure. Bare package names apply to all versions; exact versions
; joined by "||" are available when a script requires version pinning.
strict-allow-scripts=true
